d25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"ef8932d27af3f1d62c31f9e7754438ac83da821e8e3f4dcc2c74775778ce6824","event_uuid":"1ebcbae5-8bd6-4078-9e64-8657e3dd93aa","position":{"commit_sha":"2399090c7126823b1eddeca579990be08418150a","position":"1795056291048675696-1ebcbae5-8bd6-4078-9e64-8657e3dd93aa"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"badcf084136b12ede1696f7f0883db3a63d49eb08e4dff6d7b397d208b3eec2a","event_uuid":"3f4ac821-636f-4dfb-b403-27f82c6bd16c","position":{"commit_sha":"eeeb86269f1aa59886ec2f55b41b9831c3df2ea9","position":"1795059894665739567-3f4ac821-636f-4dfb-b403-27f82c6bd16c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Stopped on this bug: it needs the policy decision held by cloistered-decomposed-nymph (still open, no decision recorded). No code was changed.\n\nRoot cause (confirmed from the Windows sweep logs at b4e0d01b649): both checks read POSIX mode bits that Windows does not implement. `src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py:111` rejects `st.st_mode & 0o077`; Windows reports every file as `0o666` (dirs `0o777`), so every key is rejected (`OpcertKeyError ... 0600 or stricter (group/other bits set: mode 0o666)`, 30 tests in 7 modules). `infra/scripts/cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py` refuses its artifact directory the same way (`CleanupError: artifact directory must not be group/world accessible`, 17 tests). On Windows, file confidentiality is set by the DACL, which `os.stat` does not expose. `chmod(0o600)` in `keyprov._write_copy` also changes nothing there except the read-only bit, so a key copy inherits the parent directory's ACL.\n\nWhy this is a policy call rather than an implementation detail: an honest Windows equivalent has to decide which principals may hold access to a signing key. A user-profile file normally carries ACEs for the owner, SYSTEM and BUILTIN\\Administrators; whether those are acceptable, and whether rebar must also write a protected DACL on key copies, is exactly the question cloistered-decomposed-nymph asks. Skipping the check on Windows would silently drop the guarantee, which this bug's brief rules out.\n\nOptions:\n(1) Owner-only DACL check, OpenSSH-for-Windows rule: accept a key whose DACL grants access only to the file owner, SYSTEM and BUILTIN\\Administrators; reject any other ACE (Users, Authenticated Users, Everyone). `_write_copy` sets a protected owner-only DACL. Needs ctypes `GetNamedSecurityInfoW`/`SetNamedSecurityInfoW` code and Windows-only tests that add an `Everyone:R` ACE with `icacls` and expect rejection. Verifiable only through post-merge Windows sweeps.\n(2) Declare the op-cert service and the cleanup script Linux-only: refuse to start on Windows with an explicit error naming the missing guarantee (fail closed), and skip their tests on Windows with that reason. No key is ever loaded with an unchecked ACL.\n(3) Document reliance on the user profile's default ACL: skip the mode check on Windows and record the residual risk in the docs.\n\nDecision needed on cloistered-decomposed-nymph; this bug then implements the chosen option.","timestamp":1795038945691453814},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed as Gerrit 3440 (9771ff17b27, rebased onto 4aeb9c0fe23; the only conflict was the adjacent argfile reference lines in test.yml, both removed). make verify passed in full (exit 0) before the rebase, integration tier 226 passed, 2 skipped; after the rebase test_windows_sweep_deselect, test_ci_workflow_parity and test_windows_mode_bit_skip pass. Portability: platform branches are on os.name and Path.is_symlink only.","timestamp":1795055584145304567}],"created_at":1794857635742574816,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dec44873-0151-41ca-a9ee-95eac294f206","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6798-606d-37dc-46e7"},{"link_uuid":"2ca62077-acd0-43a8-bb9d-2c8ce2693cc9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"47d8-baf8-2348-45c9"},{"link_uuid":"1ebcbae5-8bd6-4078-9e64-8657e3dd93aa","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8bfb-5483-1291-42ae"},{"link_uuid":"3f4ac821-636f-4dfb-b403-27f82c6bd16c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b4bc-01f1-9ba0-4bcb"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job deselects 47 tests through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-permissions.args`, which this bug owns. Root cause (ticket comment, Windows logs at `b4e0d01b649`): two checks read POSIX mode bits that Windows does not implement. `src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py:111` rejects a key file with `st_mode & 0o077`; `infra/scripts/cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py:266` (`_assert_private_artifact_dir`) rejects an artifact directory the same way. Windows reports files as `0o666` and directories as `0o777`, so both always refuse there.\n\nPolicy is decided on cloistered-decomposed-nymph (option 3, operator comment 2026-11-18): on Windows rebar relies on the user profile's default ACL and documents the residual risk.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Each module gets `_POSIX_MODE_BITS = os.name != \"nt\"`, commented with the reason (Windows has no POSIX mode bits; the decision ticket). The mode check runs only when it is true. It is also the test seam, so both branches run on POSIX CI.\n- Symlink refusal in the cleanup script relies on `O_NOFOLLOW` (`cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py:167,308,366`), which Windows lacks, so a symlinked artifact is followed there. `_read_regular`, `_write_new` and `_append_record` gain a portable `path.is_symlink()` refusal before `os.open`, raising the existing \"must be a regular file\" error; `O_NOFOLLOW` stays where it exists.\n- Docs: `docs/manifest-signing.md` and `docs/comment-echo-reclaim-runbook.md` state the Windows residual risk: keys and artifacts inherit their folder's ACL; `chmod` changes only the read-only bit there; nothing checks for extra ACEs such as Users or Everyone.\n- Evidence for nymph: the `sweep (windows)` job gains a non-gating step (`continue-on-error: true`, `mechanism-ok: ci_gate` marker naming this ticket) that mints a key with `rebar._opcert_signing._generate_opcert_key` in `runner.temp` and prints `icacls` for the key and for a `tempfile.mkdtemp()` directory (where `keyprov.compose_signer`, `keyprov.py:67`, writes its copy).\n- Tests that assert POSIX modes themselves are gated on the constant: `test_rp04_s6_opcert_startup.py::test_compose_rejects_too_permissive_key_path` (`:192-201`) patches `keyprov._POSIX_MODE_BITS` to True; the copy-mode assertions at `test_rp04_s6_opcert_startup.py:242-243`, `test_opcert_service.py:177` and `test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py:114` run only when it is true; `test_cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py::test_default_run_creates_every_missing_artifact_ancestor_private` (`:323-347`) asserts `0o700` only when `cleanup._POSIX_MODE_BITS` is true and otherwise that the directories exist and the run returns 0; `test_execution_rechecks_artifact_directory_permissions_after_jira_get` (`:879-901`) skips where it is false, reason \"Windows has no POSIX mode bits; it relies on the default ACL (cloistered-decomposed-nymph)\".\n- Argfile: remove the 17 cleanup lines and 2 op-cert lines whose tests never run `ssh-keygen` (`test_opcert_key_copy_leak_tortoise.py::test_compose_signer_removes_its_dir_when_writing_the_copy_fails` and `::..._interrupted_during_validation`, which stub `_write_copy`/`_validate_key_file`, `:94,:109`). The other 28 op-cert lines go through `compose_signer`'s `ssh-keygen -y` validation (`keyprov.py:131-151`), which the Windows log shows Win32-OpenSSH refusing (\"Bad permissions ... \\\\OWNER RIGHTS (S-1-3-4)\", `test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py::test_compose_still_works_after_pop`, inline key so no mode check). That separate cause is bug plump-smelly-indianabat; those 28 lines move to its argfile `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/openssh-key-acl.args` (referenced from `.github/workflows/test.yml`) and `posix-permissions.args` is deleted.\n\nPortability: platform branches are on `os.name`; the symlink check uses `Path.is_symlink`, portable. No config key, env var or flag is added.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py`, `infra/scripts/cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_windows_mode_bit_skip.py` (new), `tests/unit/test_rp04_s6_opcert_startup.py`, `tests/unit/test_opcert_service.py`, `tests/unit/test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py`, `tests/integration/test_cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py`\n- `docs/manifest-signing.md`, `docs/comment-echo-reclaim-runbook.md`\n- `.github/workflows/test.yml`, `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-permissions.args` (deleted), `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/openssh-key-acl.args` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\n- New tests on every platform via the constants: with them false, a `0o644` key and a `0o755` artifact directory are accepted; with them true they are rejected with the existing messages; a non-regular key path is rejected either way; a symlinked artifact file is refused by the new `is_symlink` check even with `O_NOFOLLOW` patched to absent.\n- Existing POSIX tests keep running unchanged on POSIX. `make verify` and the integration tier pass.\n- After merge, a dispatched `sweep (windows)` run on main.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes, including `tests/unit/test_windows_mode_bit_skip.py`, and `pytest -m \"integration and not live\"` passes.\n- [ ] Every line removed from `posix-permissions.args` without moving names a test that passed, or skipped with the stated platform reason, in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run, and its ACL step's `icacls` output is recorded on cloistered-decomposed-nymph.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py","reason":"skip mode check on Windows"},{"path":"infra/scripts/cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py","reason":"skip mode check on Windows; portable symlink refusal"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_windows_mode_bit_skip.py","reason":"both branches tested"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_rp04_s6_opcert_startup.py","reason":"gate mode assertions"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_service.py","reason":"gate mode assertion"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py","reason":"gate mode assertion"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py","reason":"mode-asserting tests made platform-aware"},{"path":"docs/manifest-signing.md","reason":"Windows residual risk"},{"path":"docs/comment-echo-reclaim-runbook.md","reason":"Windows residual risk"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"ACL evidence step and argfile references"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-permissions.args","reason":"deleted"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/openssh-key-acl.args","reason":"op-cert lines move to plump-smelly-indianabat"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","47d8-baf8-2348-45c9"],["relates_to","8bfb-5483-1291-42ae"],["relates_to","b4bc-01f1-9ba0-4bcb"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"cbb2b571-31e9-4985-816f-8ce438aa6b20","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"44b2-e70e-2b9f-4d2a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: POSIX mode-bit checks reject keys and artifact dirs on Windows (47 tests)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["28effb22-d340-49b2-829c-de7f25f32d54","cf39373a-83aa-447d-bc8b-0612a9e6ce3a","a41ead31-03aa-408d-8314-c7293bd6ddf1","51e0ddfd-001b-4826-9e75-bc41a5a6ca3f","c5aa74c0-234c-4fac-83e4-9e9b6355699f","39343b69-c76a-4659-a9b2-611d3f8b1af9","401d1016-938b-456c-8ed4-7845011f790d","35f27e03-269b-44fd-a2c8-852b66a87e82","cbb2b571-31e9-4985-816f-8ce438aa6b20","2a7bbedf-1bb0-4a34-b59a-adfcf4ea0c87","6eba5970-9d3f-4d33-af80-72cca0c7421d","1ebcbae5-8bd6-4078-9e64-8657e3dd93aa","3f4ac821-636f-4dfb-b403-27f82c6bd16c"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795059894665739568,"uuid":"788e30e3-4bb2-4d0a-b4af-d0c71e684585"}
